# Line endings are normalized to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Why this is not optional here: several tests PARSE SOURCE FILES with regexes
# anchored on \n - the INCLUDE array in scripts/build-plugin-zip.js, the
# require.main guards in monitors/heartbeat.js and bin/handshake.js, the hook
# stdout enumeration. Windows CI checks out with core.autocrlf=true, so those
# regexes miss and the suite goes red on a tree that is byte-identical to a
# green one. It cost a full CI run to find; this is the root fix, and it also
# ends the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every git command here.
#
# The shell installer must stay LF regardless: CRLF breaks the shebang line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# One rule, deliberately. A per-extension exception is another thing to get
# wrong, and nothing here needs CRLF: the PowerShell installer is only ever
# parsed by PowerShell's own parser, which does not care.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
